// Title: LiveKD Driver Creation By Uncommon Process
// Sigma ID: 059c5af9-5131-4d8d-92b2-de4ad6146712
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth
// Description: Detects the creation of the LiveKD driver by a process image other than "livekd.exe".
// False positives:
//   - Administrators might rename LiveKD before its usage which could trigger this. Add additional names you use to the filter
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_sysinternals_livekd_driver_susp_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\LiveKdD.SYS" and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\livekd.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\livek64.exe")))
